<title>UK: SOCCER-EUROPEAN CLUB COMPETITION RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-EUROPEAN CLUB COMPETITION RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results in European club soccer</p>
<p>competitions on Wednesday:</p>
<p>UEFA Cup sacond round, first leg:</p>
<p>In Hamburg: Hamburg (Germany) 3 Spartak Moscow (Russia) 0</p>
<p>(halftime 2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Andre Breitenreiter (8), Karsten Baeron (39),</p>
<p>Marijan Kovacevic (58)</p>
<p>Attendance: 18,000</p>
<p>European Champions' League:</p>
<p>Group C</p>
<p>In Vienna: Rapid Vienna (Austria) 1 Juventus (Italy) 1</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Rapid Vienna - Andrzej Lesiak 20</p>
<p>Juventus - Christian Vieri 9</p>
<p>Attendance: 48,000</p>
<p>European Champions' League:</p>
<p>Group A</p>
<p>In Auxerre: Auxerre (France) 1 Grasshopper Zurich</p>
<p>(Switzerland) 0 (1-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Thomas Deniaud 42</p>
<p>Attendance: 19,000</p>
<p>European Champions' League:</p>
<p>Group A</p>
<p>In Amsterdam: Ajax Amsterdam (Netherlands) 4 Glasgow Rangers</p>
<p>(Scotland) 1 (2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Ajax - Dani 25 and 41, Tijani Babangida 83, Nordin Wooter 90</p>
<p>Rangers - Ian Durrant 88</p>
<p>Attendance: 47,000</p>
<p>European Champions' League:</p>
<p>Group D</p>
<p>In Gothenburg: IFK Gothenburg (Sweden) 2 AC Milan (Italy) 1</p>
<p>(0-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Gothenburg - Erik Wahlstedt 74, Niclas Alexandersson 84</p>
<p>Milan - George Weah 52</p>
<p>Attendance 42,450</p>
<p>In Trondheim: Rosenborg Trondheim (Norway) 0 Porto</p>
<p>(Portugal) 1 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Mario Jardell 90</p>
<p>Attendance: 20,400</p>
<p>Group C</p>
<p>In Istanbul: Fenerbahce (Turkey) 0 Manchester United</p>
<p>(England) 2 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: David Beckham 55, Eric Cantona 60</p>
<p>Attendence: 28,000</p>
<p>Group B</p>
<p>In Madrid: Atletico Madrid (Spain) 0 Borussia Dortmund</p>
<p>(Germany) 1 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Stefan Reuter 50</p>
<p>Attendance: 47,000</p>
<p>Group B</p>
<p>In Bucharest: Steaua Bucharest (Romania) 1 Widzew Lodz</p>
<p>(Poland) 0 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Daniel Bogusz 82, own goal</p>
<p>Attendance: 9,000</p>
</text>
